# Optional non-secret overlay environment for the LOCAL Qwen3Guard pilot profile.
#
# Combine this file AFTER the base env file, never instead of it:
#
#   docker compose \
#     --env-file .secrets/compose.env \
#     --env-file .secrets/compose.pilot.env \
#     -f compose.yaml -f compose.pilot.yaml config
#
# Later --env-file entries win for duplicate keys.  This file intentionally
# contains no generation endpoint/model settings, so the base values such as
# NASI_LEMAK_GENERATION_URL, NASI_LEMAK_GENERATION_MODEL,
# NASI_LEMAK_GENERATION_AUTH and NASI_LEMAK_GENERATION_ALLOW_INSECURE_HTTP are
# not overridden by accident.  The exact provider model ID and (for bearer auth)
# NASI_LEMAK_GENERATION_API_KEY belong in the base .secrets/compose.env only.
# The one optional non-secret generation instruction below is a reply-shape
# hint, not an endpoint or credential setting.
#
# This is the local-guard vertical.  Do NOT add any NASI_LEMAK_INPUT_GUARD_* or
# NASI_LEMAK_OUTPUT_GUARD_* hosted API settings here or combine this file with
# compose.api.yaml / compose.api-ca.yaml.  The overlay selects
# NASI_LEMAK_GUARD_BACKEND=qwen3guard-local and sets guarded mode itself; do not
# set either value again in this file.
#
# Only paths and non-secret tunables belong here.  Never put a password, a DSN
# containing a password, an application/operator key, a key digest or a model
# license value in this file, shell history, chat or Git.

# --- Read-only policy and model artifacts (host paths) ----------------------
# One operator-approved YAML policy file (see docs/policy.example.yaml for the
# exact accepted form).  Preserve each approved version under a new path.
PILOT_POLICY_FILE=/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/policy/2026-10-20.1.yaml

# Locally obtained, license-approved model directories.  The operator must
# supply the complete tokenizer/config/safetensors bundles; no model is
# downloaded by the image or at container start.
#
# The Meta directories are the already-approved pilot paths.  They remain
# REQUIRED because this overlay extends the approved Meta pilot rather than
# replacing it, even though Qwen performs the active scans.  Keep the operator's
# existing paths; do not invent new ones.
PILOT_PROMPT_GUARD_MODEL_DIR=/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/models/prompt-guard-2
PILOT_LLAMA_GUARD_MODEL_DIR=/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/models/llama-guard-3

# Qwen3Guard-Gen host directory and its required container directory.  The
# host directory is mounted read-only at the container directory, and the same
# container directory is passed to the application through
# NASI_LEMAK_QWEN3GUARD_MODEL_DIR.  Both are mandatory: Compose aborts if
# either is unset.  Qwen3Guard-Stream is not supported (it needs remote code,
# which the product rejects).  The container directory must be the fixed
# /models/qwen3guard-gen-0.6b value shown here.
PILOT_QWEN_GUARD_MODEL_DIR=/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/models/qwen3guard-gen-0.6b
PILOT_QWEN_GUARD_MODEL_CONTAINER_DIR=/models/qwen3guard-gen-0.6b

# --- Restored Meta pilot settings (uncalibrated) ----------------------------
# The threshold is a provisional decision boundary, not a calibrated accuracy
# claim.  The context limit must fit the approved Llama Guard artifact and the
# 32 reserved verdict tokens; review both against the real artifacts and the
# pilot policy before relying on this profile.
NASI_LEMAK_PROMPT_GUARD_THRESHOLD=0.5
NASI_LEMAK_LLAMA_GUARD_CONTEXT_LIMIT=4096

# --- Optional validated Qwen settings (bare pass-throughs) ------------------
# Omitted entries keep the documented application defaults.  Thresholds are a
# categorical severity floor in [0.0, 0.5], not a calibrated probability: 0.5
# blocks Controversial and Unsafe verdicts.  workers * threads must not exceed
# the CPU count; the 4-vCPU guard box defaults to 2 workers x 2 threads.  The
# long-input budget is a per-call payload budget in 512..32768; it is never
# truncated and over-budget input fails closed.
NASI_LEMAK_QWEN3GUARD_INPUT_THRESHOLD=0.5
NASI_LEMAK_QWEN3GUARD_OUTPUT_THRESHOLD=0.5
# NASI_LEMAK_QWEN3GUARD_WORKERS=2
# NASI_LEMAK_QWEN3GUARD_THREADS=2
# NASI_LEMAK_QWEN3GUARD_LONG_INPUT=8192

# --- Reply-shape settings for the pilot lane --------------------------------
# The CPU output scan costs roughly 10 s for a short reply and about 31 s for a
# ~1,000-token reply, so keep the reply well short of the work deadline.  384
# leaves room for the input and output scans; the system prompt asks for a
# concise answer.  Both are optional and non-secret.
#
# The maximum stops one request asking for a far longer reply.  The context
# budget matters as much: the guard scans the whole selected history, and on 4
# vCPU an 8192-unit context is estimated to pass the 60 s work deadline, so a
# long chat would fail on every turn.  Older messages are dropped to fit.  One
# request at a time matches the single guard worker; a second request gets an
# immediate 503 instead of queueing behind a 20 s turn.  Confirm these with the
# benchmark before treating them as final.
# NASI_LEMAK_CHAT_DEFAULT_REPLY_TOKENS=384
# NASI_LEMAK_CHAT_MAX_REPLY_TOKENS=512
# NASI_LEMAK_CHAT_CONTEXT_BUDGET=3000
# NASI_LEMAK_CHAT_MAX_CONCURRENCY=1
# NASI_LEMAK_GENERATION_SYSTEM_PROMPT=Answer concisely, in at most about 200 words, unless the user asks for more detail.

# --- Optional operational bounds --------------------------------------------
# All five are optional bare pass-throughs.  Unset keeps the application
# defaults; an explicitly invalid value makes the app live but not ready.  Chat
# concurrency is listed with the reply-shape settings above.  Values must stay
# inside the application bounds (work timeout 1..300 s, chat concurrency 1..256).
# Keep the work timeout above the longest expected turn before lowering it.
# NASI_LEMAK_CHAT_WORK_TIMEOUT=60
# NASI_LEMAK_CONTROL_CONCURRENCY=2
# NASI_LEMAK_MAX_BODY_BYTES=65536
# NASI_LEMAK_BODY_READ_TIMEOUT=5.0

# --- Provisional resource budget (not benchmarked) --------------------------
# Separate from the 512 MiB / 1 CPU lightweight default.  The adapter is
# CPU-only in this repository; no GPU support or performance claim is made.
GUARD_MEM_LIMIT=8g
GUARD_CPUS=4.0
GUARD_PIDS_LIMIT=512

# --- Distinct operator secret FILE paths ------------------------------------
# operator_key_digest: lowercase 64-hex SHA-256 digest of the operator key.
# This digest must differ from the chat application key digest.
# operator_audit_dsn: read-only reader-role PostgreSQL DSN.  It must differ
# from the runtime writer DSN in AUDIT_DSN_FILE.
#
# These are host files.  The container UID/GID 10001 must be able to read them;
# Compose local file-secret uid/gid/mode remapping is not claimed here.
OPERATOR_KEY_DIGEST_FILE=/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/.secrets/operator_key_digest
OPERATOR_AUDIT_DSN_FILE=/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/.secrets/operator_audit_dsn
